{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 1, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "Ethan blinked as the sterile white walls of his bedroom dissolved into pixels. The hum of his computer vanished, replaced by the crisp scent of pine and the distant chirp of birds. He looked down to see his hands rendered in blocky, blue-toned polygons, his plaid shirt pixelated like an old-school RPG character. The floor beneath him was now a grid of hexagonal tiles, and a floating health bar appeared in the top left corner of his vision. Panic surged as he realized—this wasn’t a dream. The game menu flickered to life, and a cheerful NPC with a top hat grinned at him. \"Welcome to Verdant Vale, traveler! Your quest log has been updated,\" it chimed before vanishing in a puff of glitter.\n\n***\n\nEthan stumbled forward, his new digital body obeying commands he didn’t consciously give. The village square materialized around him, filled with NPCs going about their routines—shopkeepers swept doorsteps, children chased a chicken, and a blacksmith hammered away at an anvil that looked suspiciously like his old coffee mug. A quest prompt dangled in his vision: *\"Defeat the Shadow in the Abandoned Mine to lift the Blight from Verdant Vale.\"* His stomach twisted; he’d never played this game before, but somehow, he knew the mine’s layout by heart. A party menu popped up, offering to add him to a team, and he cursed as he recognized his own username—*PixelPanic*—already mid-battle without his consent. He flexed his fingers, half-expecting them to pass through the air, but they clutched the hilt of a rusty sword that had materialized at his waist. The game had begun. Now he just had to survive it.", "logprobs": [{"token": "E", "logprob": -1.923073410987854}, {"token": "than", "logprob": -0.0003150205302517861}, {"token": " blinked", "logprob": -0.8956626057624817}, {"token": " as", "logprob": -2.3272182941436768}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.60733